(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The dispatch loop (doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): one loop per entry from Go, running frames until"] [4 1 "// the entry frame returns. A call of a Python function pushes its frame and continues; a return pops"] [5 1 "// it. An exception unwinds by the exception table: the covering handler's depth, lasti and target,"] [6 1 "// else the frame is left and the caller's instruction raises it."] [8 1 "// guardedStep is step with a Go panic of the runtime turned into a SystemError raised at f's instruction"] [9 1 "// (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core, PY6a's Low: a panic ended the whole lib-test module, now only its test)"] [14 17 "// the C-level checks' increments the panic skipped"] [21 1 "// run runs f (and the frames it calls) to f's return: Go's call into the machine, CPython's"] [22 1 "// _PyEval_EvalFrameDefault entered from C, the C level's recursion check first (where \"\", PY7)."] [33 1 "// runFrames is run's loop."] [37 18 "// f_back of an escaped frame reaches its callers (202b)"] [45 31 "// RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go)"] [55 4 "// f returned v"] [63 21 "// a suspended generator's f_back is None (its caller may be reused: releaseFrame)"] [75 4 "// a call of a Python function from f: run the callee in this loop"] [90 5 "// the callee's RESUME: the eval breaker (PY6f's thread_gil.go), its error raised in the callee"] [98 3 "// an exception in f at f.Lasti"] [104 4 "// an exception the runtime raised in f (a KeyError of d[k] ...): chained as _PyErr_SetObject chains"] [109 23 "// a re-raise adds no entry for the frame it is raised in (exception_unwind)"] [119 47 "// frame->instr_ptr: a reraise N's restored instruction"] [135 1 "// OpImpl implements an operation outside step's switch (PYI-SPEC.md §7.5): it pops and pushes f's"] [136 1 "// stack itself and returns (nil, nil) to go on; (nil, err) raises; (nil, *pushFrame) runs a Python"] [137 1 "// function's frame next; (v, nil) makes f return v (a generator's yield sets f.Suspended first)."] [140 1 "// opImpls are the operations registered by the files that own them (§9), each by its file's init:"] [141 1 "// RegisterOp(OpLoadAttr, ...). An operation of step's switch is never looked up here."] [144 1 "// RegisterOp sets op's implementation; a second one is a programming error (one owner per operation)."] [152 1 "// pushFrame is step's signal that the instruction called a Python function: not an exception."] [155 1 "// callStack is call [N KWNAMES]: the callable under its N arguments on f's stack (the last len(kwnames) of them"] [156 1 "// keywords), all popped; a Python function's frame (a bound method's, its self first) made from the arguments"] [157 1 "// where they are on the stack and returned as the thread's *pushFrame, a generator made, or any other callable"] [158 1 "// called and its value pushed (202b: the arguments were copied off the stack, then again with self in front)."] [167 24 "// the callable's slot holds self: the arguments are self's and the stack's"] [188 3 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [192 24 "// read by runFrames before the thread's next call"] [196 1 "// kwnamesAt is a call's keyword names, the tuple constant i of str (-1: none), made once."] [218 1 "// step runs f's instructions until it returns (the value, nil), raises (nil, error), or calls a"] [219 1 "// Python function (nil, *pushFrame)."] [223 25 "// compiled ahead (PY8, aot.go): the same frame, from f.PC"] [592 6 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [631 33 "// a function made where the globals are a mapping has them too (func_globals)"] [650 52 "// JUMP_BACKWARD: the eval breaker"] [681 24 "// FOR_ITER clears a raised StopIteration: the loop's end"] [703 5 "// RERAISE N: the lasti N items down is where the frame reports itself (f_lineno)"] [709 4 "// the traceback continues: the handler's frame is already in it"]